  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/20fae49e-9ca1-4966-bb06-93bd6b8baf79-image.png\" style=\"width: 296px; height: 200px;\" /></p><p>Given, the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;on the line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Let, the point of&nbsp;intersection of the two lines be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math></p><p>Then, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;can be taken as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>7</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Given, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;units and the distance between the points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msqrt><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msqrt><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><mn>36</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>The slope of a line joining the points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>If we take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>And, the slope of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>If we take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>And, the slope of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></p>",
